plumb began as a port of pstack
(https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack), Copyright (c) 2026 Lauren Tan,
licensed under the MIT License. pstack is where plumb's shape came from: the idea
of a router that indexes named principles, the decision to keep principles as
plain documents rather than skills, and most of the principle names still in use.

principles/ holds 22 files. Of those, 0 are reproduced verbatim from pstack —
every one has been rewritten in plumb's own words, in Japanese, stating why the
principle is hard to keep and how to tell whether it was kept. Each carries
`origin: plumb` in its frontmatter. The English names survive because the
playbooks cite them by name.

The playbooks are likewise written for plumb, not translated: docs/scope.md
records, for each one, what it took from pstack and where it departs.

scripts/check-harness.sh verifies the counts above against the files themselves,
so the sentence cannot drift when a principle is added or changed.
